"""Descriptive reports from saved evaluation outputs; never changes inference rules."""
import hashlib,json
from collections import Counter
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
if __name__=='__main__':
    summary=json.loads((ROOT/'evaluation/summary.json').read_text());reports=summary['reports'];rows=json.loads((ROOT/'evaluation/results/qwen-v3-rubric-policy/comparison.json').read_text());candidate=reports['qwen-v3-rubric-policy'];changes=json.loads((ROOT/'evaluation/predictions/qwen-v3-paired-policy/derivation.json').read_text())['changes']
    report='''# Human evaluation — 50 reviews\n\nAll 50 topic/intent/severity answers are complete and valid. All three frozen configurations produced 50 valid predictions with no missing records. Human answers were unchanged, used only for offline scoring and descriptive inspection, and never sent to inference models or used to tune prompts/rules. The candidate policy and configurations were frozen before inspecting these errors.\n\n| Frozen configuration | Topic agreement | Intent agreement | Severity exact | Severity MAE | All three correct |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'''
    for name in ('gemma-baseline','qwen-v2-frozen','qwen-v3-rubric-policy'):
        r=reports[name];report+=f"| {name} | {r['accuracy']['topic']:.0%} | {r['accuracy']['intent']:.0%} | {r['accuracy']['severity']:.0%} | {r['severity_mae_completed']:.2f} | {r['all_three_correct']}/50 |\n"
    report+='''\nQwen improves topic and intent agreement relative to Gemma on this set. The rubric-only v3 policy improves Qwen severity agreement from 60% to 66% and reduces its MAE from 0.54 to 0.46. Gemma's severity-only MAE remains lower (0.40), so this is not an improvement on every metric. Four Qwen predictions were adjusted by the pre-frozen complaint-severity rule; all are flagged for review and the raw model responses remain saved. The paired offline calculation produces the same metrics as independently executed v3 inference.\n\n| Configuration | Topic macro F1, all 8 | Intent macro F1, all 5 | Topic F1, supported classes | Intent F1, supported classes |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n'''
    for name in ('gemma-baseline','qwen-v2-frozen','qwen-v3-rubric-policy'):
        r=reports[name];report+=f"| {name} | {r['macro_f1']['topic']:.6f} | {r['macro_f1']['intent']:.6f} | {r['topic']['macro_f1_supported_labels']:.6f} | {r['intent']['macro_f1_supported_labels']:.6f} |\n"
    report+='''\nThere are no human examples labeled access, downloads, support, or cancellation. The all-label macro F1 assigns zero to absent undefined classes; the supported-class version avoids implying those categories were evaluated. Other human fields (sentiment, entities, evidence quote, needs_review) are blank, so no human accuracy for them is invented. Every prediction quote is anchored to its original source text.\n\nThe inference isolation audit checked 146 new attempts and their frozen prompts/settings. Four Gemma predictions reused exact same-configuration saved results; no reuse crosses configurations. Timestamp formatting in the human spreadsheet changed to minute resolution. IDs and texts match; canonical supplied source values preserve exact row hashes.\n\nThe runnable improved profile is `pipeline/configs/qwen-v3.json`. It was selected on the pre-existing development evidence, not the human scores: rubric consistency, synthetic 11/12, injection cases unchanged, and no changes to the other 97 development-pilot outputs. `pipeline/run.py --profile qwen-v3` loads this profile; Gemma remains available explicitly for reproducibility. All pre-existing corpus classifications and cost measurements remain preserved. A new configuration invalidates prior classification caches; it does not relabel historical results silently.\n\nScaling remains on hold. There are 14 topic, 9 intent, and 17 severity disagreements on the v3 candidate, with only 22/50 matching all three. This is a small diagnostic benchmark, not evidence of validated full-corpus accuracy. Additional improvements must use independent development data and a fresh holdout; these 50 answers must not become optimization targets.\n\nArtifacts: `summary.json`, each `results/<name>/report.json`, per-record `comparison.json`, confusion CSVs, `ERROR_ANALYSIS.md`, `frozen/improvement-plan.json`, and `isolation-audit.json`. Recompute without a model with `python3 evaluation/run_evaluation.py`. Additional cash expenditure for these local evaluations is $0.\n'''
    (ROOT/'evaluation/REPORT.md').write_text(report)
    signed=Counter(r['prediction']['severity']-r['human']['severity'] for r in rows);topic_pairs=Counter((r['human']['topic'],r['prediction']['topic']) for r in rows if 'topic' in r['error_fields'])
    analysis=f'''# Error inspection — descriptive, not tuning input\n\nThe frozen Qwen v3 candidate disagrees with one or more human labels on {sum(bool(r['error_fields']) for r in rows)} of 50 reviews. Human labels are the scoring reference and remain unchanged; the observations below do not remove disagreements or revise scores. No classifier change was made in response to these errors.\n\nSeverity agrees on {signed[0]} records. It is higher than the human label on {sum(n for value,n in signed.items() if value>0)} and lower on {sum(n for value,n in signed.items() if value<0)}. There are {sum(n for value,n in signed.items() if abs(value)>=2)} differences of two severity levels, all overestimates. Cases involving playback blocks, restricted controls and prices account for several severity disagreements; the exact row-level evidence is in `results/qwen-v3-rubric-policy/comparison.json`.\n\n| Topic discrepancy: human → model | Count |\n|---|---:|\n'''
    for pair,n in topic_pairs.most_common():analysis+=f"| {pair[0]} → {pair[1]} | {n} |\n"
    analysis+='''\nSpecific cases worth inspection:\n\n| Review ID | Observation | Interpretation retained for review |\n|---|---|---|\n| `16d640e9-b281-4746-9562-c7dbcf7126b6` | Premium-only basic features were predicted as account access. | A clear topic-boundary failure to document; no ID-specific exception or prompt example was added. |\n| `2aa566c6-b98d-4513-b900-83702a8db8eb` | A positive review explicitly mentioning reduced advertising was predicted as other. | The model missed a specific praised feature. |\n| `ac6cd66d-a9d2-42a4-afb8-2f84beff7fd1` | Human catalog/praise differs from model other/unclear, with needs_review true. | Short non-English content remains a limitation; no translation or expected answer was supplied to the model. |\n| `01d453b0-dca3-42e9-8aa4-5fc167b08070` | An ironic ad-related review is human unclear/severity 1 versus model complaint/severity 3. | Sarcasm and supported impact are ambiguous. Neither answer is silently changed. |\n| `723f07de-9881-4049-8680-1a9e25652914` | A resolved update plus an older crash account has different intent interpretations. | Time ordering and mixed historical/current experience complicate the primary intent. |\n\nSome mismatches also merit checking the human annotation against the written contract; these remain scored mismatches, not automatically excused model errors:\n\n| Review ID | Rubric question |\n|---|---|\n| `a70e8d3e-3f84-46bc-b008-67f476c67963` | Human usability vs model other for general praise; the contract assigns general praise to other unless a feature is supported. |\n| `b58dd6f0-ad88-4319-b6db-58afb60c37c1` | Human playback vs model usability for organizing saved albums/artists; playlist/library management is listed under usability. |\n| `3ddb3f4e-f7b9-430b-b335-eadc6d321f46` | Human complaint vs model cancellation when the reviewer explicitly says they are deleting the app; the intent hierarchy gives explicit leaving precedence. Its topic is separately disputed. |\n| `ac4e860a-c042-49cc-90f3-189591c336ac` | Human billing vs model downloads for failed offline playback while paying; a paid-plan mention alone does not define billing. |\n\nThese questions do not authorize changing your answers, introducing accepted alternatives after seeing predictions, or training on these rows. If annotations are independently adjudicated later, preserve both label versions and recompute a separately versioned report.\n\nThe only implemented change was frozen before this inspection: complaint severity 1 becomes severity 2 and is flagged needs_review. It leaves topic and intent untouched, never raises cancellation intent alone, preserves raw output, and changes the cache fingerprint. It corrects a semantic inconsistency without pretending to solve the remaining topic, language, sarcasm and impact errors. No human row was added to a model prompt or development test.\n'''
    (ROOT/'evaluation/ERROR_ANALYSIS.md').write_text(analysis)
    decision={'status':'hold_before_scaling','approved_scope':'50 frozen text-only evaluation predictions plus same-size 100-review development smoke test','classifier_profile':'qwen-v3','profile_selected_on':'pre-existing development validation and contract-only semantic rule, not human score optimization','human_answers_used_for_tuning':False,'human_labels_unchanged':True,'remaining_disagreements':candidate['error_counts'],'full_field_matches':candidate['all_three_correct'],'10k_started':False,'full_run_started':False,'cash_spend_usd':0,'reason':'Substantial remaining disagreements and annotation ambiguities are documented; do not extrapolate a small diagnostic set into a claim of full-corpus quality.'}
    (ROOT/'evaluation/scale-decision.json').write_text(json.dumps(decision,indent=2)+'\n')
    print('Wrote evaluation/REPORT.md, ERROR_ANALYSIS.md, and scale-decision.json')
